INTERPRETER IDENTITY
Before the PUC KAT, the fixed tools/bin/lua51 path must satisfy both
rawget(_G, "jit") == nil and _VERSION == "Lua 5.1". The already positively
identified LuaJIT full-run interpreter is run against the same predicate and
must fail it, providing a cheap negative selftest without copying an
interpreter or overwriting any file.

POSITIVE COVERAGE
The full run projected and inspected all 38 zones, all 57 public land routes,
and all 4 public boat routes. Land classes are exactly 30 primary, 24
secondary and 3 trail. It pins numeric/id order, complete literal first,
middle and last zone and land-route records, every boat record, every zone's
primary_relief_id, the three record schemas and exact bucket rosters. It
reconstructs every relevant Source record losslessly, including false versus
real non-empty text for faction and both optional gate references. It also
proves Source immutability and absence of mutable aliases in or from output.

The harness-only complete compiled-data shell contains all 21 existing
geometry families, with the three D-1 families inserted and every other
geometry family empty.
The reserved island_routes family is explicitly empty. The shell includes the
real typed selectors, spatial, coverage and release sections, and passes only
through compiled_schema.canonicalize_compiled. Its canonical bytes and the
three family arrays are hashed by the real canonical encoder/hasher. The shell
digest is an acceptance-harness digest, not a production compiler-output digest.

NEGATIVE COVERAGE
The full run rejects a non-plain dependency table and unknown dependency;
missing and additional Source fields; empty faction text; metatables; sparse
arrays; mutable aliases; cycles; wrong types; NaN, positive infinity, negative
infinity, fractional and out-of-range integers; direct zone and boat count
drift; direct zone and boat numeric/order drift; empty biome arrays; duplicate
biome IDs; a crossing station outside its centreline; reordered, duplicate and
changed route identities; numeric and empty-string optional gate references;
land_058 boundary-only contamination;
island-route contamination; and an injected Source-validator failure before
package-local validation. A same-shape mutation is rejected by the real Source
checksum; with the explicit accepting test seam the same mutation moves the
complete-shell digest. The real canonicalizer rejects a compiled schema
identity mismatch, a negative unsigned value, unsorted named rows and a
mutable alias. Focused records plus cases are 184, below the 300 cap.

The duplicate route-identity mutant runs behind the explicit accepting
validator seam: Stage 1 remains the owner of Source identity uniqueness, while
D-1 rejects the current route_001-to-route_002 mutant through its exact
position-to-route_NNN check. No second generic uniqueness rule was added.

